1
00:00:00,370 --> 00:00:05,370
Hey everyone, today we're talking about the Push-Pull Converter.

2
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:11,370
A Push-Pull is a two-transistor converter, highly efficient, runs on low voltage power.

3
00:00:11,370 --> 00:00:17,540
The main power components of this converter are two transistors.

4
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:27,610
They drive a center tapped winding, and then we get the result at the output across the load.

5
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:31,610
But for our system, a standard Push-Pull just won't cut it.

6
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:34,610
We've got a few differences.

7
00:00:34,610 --> 00:00:40,610
Our system runs on natural energy, so the Push-Pull will also be adapted a bit for that purpose.

8
00:00:40,610 --> 00:00:50,100
Here we've got a prototype circuit that we're going to test, the control board.

9
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:54,100
The timing IC used is the TL494.

10
00:00:54,100 --> 00:01:01,100
You can also use the SG3525, UC3825, and others.

11
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:06,100
Pretty much any chip with a duty cycle adjustment will work.

12
00:01:06,100 --> 00:01:15,100
The driver was specifically chosen at 2A, the IR2113, to show that regular drivers work just fine in this system.

13
00:01:15,100 --> 00:01:20,100
Here we've got two transistors bolted to heatsinks.

14
00:01:20,100 --> 00:01:25,100
And everybody's favorite, the well-known pot core transformer from old TV sets.

15
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:28,440
Let's walk through the schematic.

16
00:01:28,440 --> 00:01:34,820
This is the kind of support circuit the Push-Pull needs to run.

17
00:01:34,820 --> 00:01:37,820
No need to overthink it, or get clever.

18
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:47,610
The key thing is our transistor, the IRFP260N, or similar high-voltage transistors.

19
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:49,610
Why high voltage?

20
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:55,610
In this system, there's a static spike that appears during operation.

21
00:01:55,610 --> 00:02:03,610
And if the transistor is low voltage, well, the body diode inside it is also rated low voltage by the manufacturer.

22
00:02:03,610 --> 00:02:07,610
And it'll clip the static spike and turn it into heat.

23
00:02:07,610 --> 00:02:09,610
We don't want that.

